Title: Tracker music through libmodplug
Repository: love
Base: def245102c67909f9902095af613b1ae05249b62
Requires: preceding patches in series
Date: 2026-11-20
Author: aros-loeve project
Problem: The AROS build left out libmodplug (patch 0003), so games with tracker music (MOD, S3M, XM, IT) had none: love.sound.newDecoder failed for these files.
Change: libmodplug 0.8.9.0 is built with the other libraries (scripts/deps.py; version and options of AROS contrib's recipe) and linked statically; LOVE_NO_MODPLUG is no longer set on AROS and the build looks for libmodplug again.
Scope: AROS (all targets)
Upstream: local-only
Verification: mainline x86_64 (nightly 2026-11-15), 2026-11-20: a generated 4-channel module with a rising scale opens as 44100 Hz stereo, duration 8.00 s, and plays as a stream; the emulated sound card's recorded output holds 8 s of signal whose pitch rises from about 290 to 500 Hz second by second. Not run: Raspberry Pi, formats other than MOD.
Removal: not planned
---
diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 240e9d7b78a3d15bf13c764d03d545f03da68f20..c543743ddb460cdb81da8b937320edfebfedc6e2 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -203,10 +203,11 @@ Please see https://github.com/love2d/megasource
 		target_link_libraries(lovedep::OpenAL INTERFACE SDL3::SDL3)
 	endif()
 
-	if(NOT LOVE_AROS)
 	find_package(ModPlug REQUIRED)
 	target_include_directories(lovedep::Modplug INTERFACE ${MODPLUG_INCLUDE_DIR})
 	target_link_libraries(lovedep::Modplug INTERFACE ${MODPLUG_LIBRARY})
+	if(LOVE_AROS)
+		target_compile_definitions(lovedep::Modplug INTERFACE MODPLUG_STATIC)
 	endif()
 
 	find_package(Theora REQUIRED)
diff --git a/src/common/config.h b/src/common/config.h
